## Why This Is Asked

This question tests the ability to design streaming algorithms with bounded memory while computing exact results. It captures a common real-world problem: maintaining aggregate statistics over a sliding or growing dataset without storing all historical values.

## Key Concepts

- **Streaming data structures:** Using heaps to maintain top-K elements efficiently
- **Running sum:** Incremental updates avoid recomputing the sum after each batch
- **Time complexity:** O(log K) per element; batch processing takes O(B log K)
- **Memory usage:** O(K) vs O(N) for the exact method that stores all past values

## Code Example

```javascript
function topKSumStream(valueStream, K) {
  const heap = new MinHeap();
  let sum = 0;

  for (const batch of valueStream) {
    for (const v of batch) {
      if (heap.size() < K) {
        heap.push(v);
        sum += v;
      } else if (heap.size() > 0 && v > heap.peek()) {
        sum += v - heap.pop();
        heap.push(v);
      }
    }
    console.log("Top-K sum:", sum);
  }
}
```

## Asymptotic Analysis

| Metric | Our Solution | Exact Method |
|--------|--------------|--------------|
| Per-element update | O(log K) | O(1) |
| Batch time (size B) | O(B log K) | O(B) |
| Memory | O(K) | O(N) |

## Why This Is Asked
Tests mastery of amortized batching, range updates, and exact coverage checks on a line, common in streaming analytics and scheduling systems.

## Key Concepts
- Coordinate compression, segment tree with range updates, global min check, amortized batching, space efficiency.

## Code Example
```javascript
class SegTree {
  constructor(n){ this.n=n; this.min=Array(4*n).fill(0); this.cover=Array(4*n).fill(0); this.lazy=Array(4*n).fill(0); }
  _apply(i,delta){ this.cover[i]+=delta; this.min[i]+=delta; this.lazy[i]+=delta; }
  _push(i){ if(this.lazy[i]!==0){ this._apply(i*2,this.lazy[i]); this._apply(i*2+1,this.lazy[i]); this.lazy[i]=0; } }
  update(qL,qR,delta,i=1,l=0,r=this.n-1){ if(qR<l||r<qL) return; if(qL<=l&&r<=qR){ this._apply(i,delta); return; } this._push(i); const m=(l+r)>>1; this.update(qL,qR,delta,i*2,l,m); this.update(qL,qR,delta,i*2+1,m+1,r); this.min[i]=Math.min(this.min[i*2],this.min[i*2+1]); }
  fullCovered(){ return this.min[1]>0; }
}
``` 

